<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Avantivarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 855–883</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Avantivarman was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> from 855 to 883 and founder of the Utpala dynasty, which replaced the Karkota line. His reign was remembered as a time of recovery: his engineer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suyya">Suyya</a> drained marshes and regulated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhelum">Jhelum</a> to win new farmland, and he founded the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avantipur">Avantipura</a> with its temples. His court patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poets and critics such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anandavardhana">Anandavardhana</a>.</p></div>
